Subject: Check an empty function wrapper before storage dispatch

Local compatibility guard for libc++ 10.0.1; not an upstream backport.
Responds to a downstream GCC 13 nonnull diagnostic. That exact diagnostic has
NOT been independently reproduced. The null-first form preserves cleanup for
empty, inline and heap storage; callable lifetime tests pass under GCC/Clang.
Keep separate from the reproduced fixes so maintainers can evaluate or drop it
independently. No warning suppression is introduced.

--- a/functional
+++ b/functional
@@ -1822,8 +1822,10 @@
     _LIBCPP_INLINE_VISIBILITY
     ~__value_func()
     {
+        if (!__f_)
+            return;
         if ((void*)__f_ == &__buf_)
             __f_->destroy();
-        else if (__f_)
+        else
             __f_->destroy_deallocate();
     }
